# core.autocrlf is true on the Windows machine, and Git decides text vs binary
# by sniffing the first few KB. It gets the PNGs, the fonts and most of the
# rulebook PDFs right, but it reads reportlab's print-and-play PDFs as TEXT -
# `git ls-files --eol` showed i/lf on all four - so a fresh clone rewrote every
# LF byte in them to CRLF. The files grew by 470 bytes, every cross-reference
# offset moved, and the PDFs came out of the clone damaged: tolerant readers
# recovered them through "incorrect startxref pointer", strict ones need not.
# Caught 2026-10-28. The stored blobs were always correct; only checkout was
# corrupting them, so marking the types here is the whole fix.
#
# Do not rely on sniffing for a binary type. Name it.

*.pdf  binary
*.png  binary
*.ttf  binary
*.docx binary
